WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.480
I wanted to see inside a developing zebrafish. These

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:12.360
photographs are from an experiment that did not work.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:18.321
The specimens were tiny. A small change in orientation

00:00:18.321 --> 00:00:20.440
could decide whether

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:26.089
a section passed through the anatomy I needed, or

00:00:26.089 --> 00:00:28.280
missed it entirely.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:36.440
My plan was to hold each specimen in a two percent

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.190
agarose matrix. That support would establish

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:44.280
orientation before subsequent tissue processing.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:49.984
After dehydration and clearing, paraffin was meant to

00:00:49.984 --> 00:00:52.930
provide sufficient mechanical

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:59.395
support for microtomy. On paper, each material had a

00:00:59.395 --> 00:01:01.260
reasonable job.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:06.339
But a hydrophilic gel and a hydrophobic embedding

00:01:06.339 --> 00:01:08.950
medium do not automatically

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:13.882
form a mechanically coherent block. Their interface

00:01:13.882 --> 00:01:16.300
was the vulnerable point.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:21.667
The processed block formed distinguishable layers. At

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:24.440
the microtome, they separated

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:29.667
and broke apart. A usable ribbon of histological

00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:32.280
sections never appeared.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:38.451
The failure involved the materials, not simply the

00:01:38.451 --> 00:01:40.440
machine. But what

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:45.293
I could observe was separation. Its precise physical

00:01:45.293 --> 00:01:48.280
explanation remained unresolved.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:54.087
The grade and thermal behaviour of agarose might have

00:01:54.087 --> 00:01:55.950
contributed. I did

00:01:55.950 --> 00:02:01.172
not establish that experimentally, and the photographs

00:02:01.172 --> 00:02:03.300
alone cannot prove it.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.646
A future comparison could examine agarose grade,

00:02:07.646 --> 00:02:11.440
concentration and processing conditions, then

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:16.021
measure block integrity during sectioning. Those are

00:02:16.021 --> 00:02:19.280
proposals, not completed experiments.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:24.247
No interpretable section came from this attempt. I

00:02:24.247 --> 00:02:24.990
kept the

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:29.832
photographs anyway. The failed block was the evidence

00:02:29.832 --> 00:02:30.380
I had.
